    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "WP\nWestern Pacific\nAIRLINES\n737\nFor your safety...\nGovernment regulations require that a passenger seated in a designated exit seat\nnotify a crew member prior to departure if: You do not read, speak or understand\nthe language in which your flight crew delivered the pre-flight briefing.\nPara su seguridad....\nLos reglamentos del gobierno requieren que un pasajero sentado en un\nasiento designado de salida de emergencia, le haga saber a un miembro de\nla tripulación antes de la salida del vuelo si no puede leer, hablar o entender\nel idioma en el que los miembros de la tripulación la dieron las instrucciones\nprevias al vuelo.\nEXIT ROW SEATING REGULATIONS\nTo sit in an emergency exit seat, you must:\n1. Read English well enough to understand the instructions for opening exits\nand for other emergency procedures.\n2. See well enough to read these instructions, see hand signals given by\ncrew members, and look outside for dangers such as smoke, fire or water\nwhich would make the exit unusable. You can wear eyeglasses or contact\n3. Hear well enough to understand English commands. You can use a hearing aid\n4. Speak well enough to give information in English to crew members or other\npassengers during an emergency.\n5. Have the strength, mobility, or dexterity to quickly open the exit and assist other\npassengers through the exit and away from the plane. Some window hatches\nthat must be lifted weigh as much as 65 pounds (the approximate weight of a 7\nyear old child).\n6. Be at least 15 years old.\n7. Have no other responsibilities, such as caring for a small child, that would distract\nyou from occupying an emergency exit row seat.\nYou must be willing and able to do all of these things by yourself and without\ncausing harm to yourself. If you are unwilling or unable (due to a discernible\nor nondiscernible condition) to accept the prescribed responsibilities, you\ncannot occupy an emergency exit row seat. If you are already seated there,\nask a crew member or customer service agent to assist you to another seat.\nYou do not have to explain why.\nPlease obey the \"No Smoking\" and \"Fasten Seatbelt\" signs\nand all instructions given by your crew members.\nFOR THE SAFETY OF FUTURE PASSENGERS\nPLEASE DO NOT REMOVE THIS CARD FROM THE AIRCRAFT.\nPARA LA SEGURIDAD DE PASAJEROS FUTUROS, POR FAVOR\nNO RETIRE ESTA TARJETA DEL AVION.",
      "In the event of an emergency, follow the\ndirections and hand signals of your crew.\nIf a crewmember is not available to assist\nyou, follow the instructions on the \"Safety\nInstructions\" card and posted signs. Wait\nuntil the airplane has stopped before\nopening the exit and look through the\nwindow, assessing conditions (looking for\nsmoke, fire or obstructions) to determine\nwhether it is safe to proceed. If it is safe\nto do so, operate the exit and assist\nothers according to the instructions.\nAssess, select and follow a safe path\naway from the airplane.\nYour Flight Attendants will be glad to\nanswer any questions you may have.\nWP\nWestern Pacific\nAIRLINES",
      "RESTRICTED AT ALL TIMES\nNO Tampering\nwith lavatory smok\ntectors is a Federal Offense\nEXIT\nB\nEXIT\nB\nEXIT\nC 1995 SAFEAIR, INC.\n95052"
    ],
